{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey","id":1068229,"title":"[2E] Astral \u2013 How long take journey?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-26T03:39:09-07:00","id":1068229,"title":"[2E] Astral \u2013 How long take journey?","content":"In my last \u2018London\u2019 game session, PCs started conflict with witch hunters over site of Iris to Anima Mundi. Hunters made call for the backup, but on site was taken out by players later. As in something like 15 minutes I suppose will be two helicopters of military hunters -<b> If PCs start Astral travel over Anima Mundi, how much time will it take them? How much should players ASSUME journey should take ( they PCs are rather experienced Pentacle mages )?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-26-2017, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:11:15-07:00","id":1068250,"title":"","content":"If they're not in the Astral yet then meditation in will take too long. Inside the Astral travel time varies, but usually lines up roughly with real world travel time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:15:04-07:00","id":1068252,"title":"","content":"You can skip meditation with a Mind however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:21:36-07:00","id":1068255,"title":"","content":"If you have Mind then just use One Mind Two Thoughts and get your physical bodies out of there while still hanging out in the Astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:27:21-07:00","id":1068258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068255#post1068255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have Mind then just use One Mind Two Thoughts and get your physical bodies out of there while still hanging out in the Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.160</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">+2 Reach: When in the Astral Realms, one of the actions<br /> may be purely \u201cPhysical.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Quote marks on &quot;Physical&quot; indicate that it's not normal physical action but one that takes place in Astral. It would be too much for a first dot spell, but nothing stops you from doing some Weaving with this function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:34:58-07:00","id":1068261,"title":"","content":"They have Mind 4 Mastigos with them - would character be possible to sustain their Astral travel WHEN they also prepare to physical combat with witch hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:41:09-07:00","id":1068263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068261#post1068261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have Mind 4 Mastigos with them - would character be possible to sustain their Astral travel WHEN they also prepare to physical combat with witch hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to Make or Unmake anything to do this, don't you? So the answer is 'yes'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:41:16-07:00","id":1068264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068250#post1068250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're not in the Astral yet then meditation in will take too long. Inside the Astral travel time varies, but usually lines up roughly with real world travel time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astral takes instant access with Mind spell ( probably 3rd dot ) and the roughly the same time as journey inside Inner Realms? <br /> <br /> Whoa, journey looks like it will takes at least 'day' of Astral time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So I suspect they need to prepare resistance first - or they will be both attacked in Material and Astral world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:02:34-07:00","id":1068266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068258#post1068258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quote marks on &quot;Physical&quot; indicate that it's not normal physical action but one that takes place in Astral. It would be too much for a first dot spell, but nothing stops you from doing some Weaving with this function.</div> </div> </div> </div>That spell is the entire foundation for the DreamSpeaker legacy, so I don't buy that. Actually, let me clarify further, in the Astral -all- of your actions are technically mental actions including the &quot;Physical&quot; ones, that's what the Reach option does, allows you to take an Instant Mental and Instant Physical action at the same time in the Astral. The base version of the spell allows you to split your attention between the Fallen and the Astral and you only get to act in one or the other each turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-26-2017, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:04:56-07:00","id":1068268,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> if they're split between the Astral and Fallen then each turn they can take action in only one or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T07:09:34-07:00","id":1068282,"title":"","content":"About time passing in the Astral: I believe the Astral Realms book said that the time spent in the Astral lines up roughly with IRL time regardless of how long time the characters perceive in the Astral.<br /> Whatever you do in the Astral will seem to take an appropriate amount of time while in the Astral. However, the time that passes in the material is equal to the amount of IRL time it takes for the players and ST to narrate what happens in the Astral.<br /> So if the characters walk for hours in the Astral but it only takes five minutes to narrate it, it only takes five minutes in the material. And if the characters has an intense fight that takes ten rounds (basically half a minute) but an hour passes IRL because there's a lot of discussion and dice rolling and descriptions and whatnot, the entire half-minute fight will take place over an hour in the material.<br /> <br /> Edit: I like it a lot, but unfortunately it's fucking ass to try to run it that way if you allow players to take action in both the Astral and material during the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-26-2017, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:44:53-07:00","id":1068310,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was one of the cutest ideas in Astral Realms and a great way to bring it home how perceptual time works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T09:58:14-07:00","id":1068328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068266#post1068266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That spell is the entire foundation for the DreamSpeaker legacy, so I don't buy that. Actually, let me clarify further, in the Astral -all- of your actions are technically mental actions including the &quot;Physical&quot; ones, that's what the Reach option does, allows you to take an Instant Mental and Instant Physical action at the same time in the Astral. The base version of the spell allows you to split your attention between the Fallen and the Astral and you only get to act in one or the other each turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This legacy is from 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T11:16:14-07:00","id":1068350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068328#post1068328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This legacy is from 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it did, how is that relevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T13:09:33-07:00","id":1068389,"title":"","content":"And its based on different mechanics. As it is written now it doesn't allow for astral travel.<br /> I'll show you.<br /> I love going to theater and &quot;watch&quot; movies with my girlfriend. - means that I don't in fact watch any movies there<br /> When in the Astral Realms, one of the actions may be purely \u201cPhysical.\u201d - means that action is not entirelly Physical which indicates that it must be undertaken in Astral<br /> <br /> Edit: Or maybe I just copy quirks from my native language and interpret it wrong. Compelling seems to be not enough to be in two dimensions at once, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-26-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T14:20:10-07:00","id":1068413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068389#post1068389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Or maybe I just copy quirks from my native language and interpret it wrong. Compelling seems to be not enough to be in two dimensions at once, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the point of the reach option. You can get lower level spells to do what seems to be a higher purpose with reach (at least some of the time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T14:27:12-07:00","id":1068416,"title":"","content":"It is kind of weird that &quot;Physical&quot; is in quotation marks, as the context does appear to indicate that the word in quotation is being used ironically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T15:14:17-07:00","id":1068436,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7825\" data-vbnamecard=\"7825\">Falcon777</a> Being able to do one physical action that contains itself in astral is also a better version of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T15:52:20-07:00","id":1068451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068389#post1068389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And its based on different mechanics. As it is written now it doesn't allow for astral travel.<br /> I'll show you.<br /> I love going to theater and &quot;watch&quot; movies with my girlfriend. - means that I don't in fact watch any movies there<br /> When in the Astral Realms, one of the actions may be purely \u201cPhysical.\u201d - means that action is not entirelly Physical which indicates that it must be undertaken in Astral<br /> <br /> Edit: Or maybe I just copy quirks from my native language and interpret it wrong. Compelling seems to be not enough to be in two dimensions at once, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're focusing on the wrong thing about the quotation marks, the split in attention allows you to have one thought track in the Fallen, and one thought track in the Astral. You could simultaneously carry on a conversation in both realms at the same time, or you could perform one physical action in the Fallen or one &quot;Physical&quot; action in the Astral. With the Reach, you can perform a &quot;Physical&quot; action in the Astral at the same time as a mental action in either the Fallen or the Astral. For instance you could throw a punch in the Astral while narrating the fight in the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T19:08:28-07:00","id":1068508,"title":"","content":"Couldn't you use Time to tweak it so that fifteen years in the Astral only takes fifteen seconds in the physical world? Or even Mind, if time is a construct of perception in the Astral Realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T01:39:50-07:00","id":1068581,"title":"","content":"<b>One Mind, Two Thoughts (Mind \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Expression, Science<br /> The subject may hold two individual and wholly distinct trains<br /> of thought at once, <b>as long as neither is physically demanding</b>.<br /> She can perform two separate Mental or Social extended tasks<br /> at the same time. <b>Neither task can be a purely Physical task</b>,<br /> but the subject can carry on a conversation while composing a<br /> sonnet, or write a poem while researching scientific discoveries.<br /> <b>The subject is incapable of multitasking spells, as they are <u>more<br /> than just an exercise of consciousness.</u></b><br /> +1 Reach: The subject may perform two separate Mental<br /> instant tasks at the same time.<br /> +2 Reach:<b> When in the Astral Realms</b>, one of the actions<br /> may be purely \u201cPhysical.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Base spell forbids Physical actions. Also doesn't allow spellcasting since it's &quot;more than just an exercise of consciousness&quot; - Being in Astral is also more than just an exercise of consciousness&quot;, imo.<br /> Notion of &quot;Physical&quot;(as in &quot;not purely Physical&quot;) appears only in Reach effect saying about being in Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T04:06:32-07:00","id":1068603,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> no it forbids performing a physical task at the same time that you're trying to maintain two separate thoughts. You can still perform physical actions over the course of the spell. So if you were maintaining consciousness in the Fallen and the Astral and you got into a fist fight in either realm then one of your streams of consciousness would freeze while the remaining stream would concentrate on the fight. After the fight if the spell hasn't run out of Duration you can resume paying attention to your split streams of thought in both realms. The exception is if you have the fist fight in the Astral and the Reach clause active to allow simultaneous &quot;Physical&quot; actions in which case you can fist fight in the Astral and perform a simultaneous mental action in either realm.<br /> <br /> Again, this spell is what becomes the most basic ability of Dreamspeakers who are supposed to be able to exist in the Astral and the Fallen at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-27-2017, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T05:54:30-07:00","id":1068626,"title":"","content":"Isnt being in the astral more than just a train of thought tho? Id personally only allow acting in both realms at the same time at higher than mind 1, maybe even not till mastery/making spell that creates a copy of you in the astral. The whole physical thing means that if you have the spell up in the astral you can do a &quot;physical action&quot; and another mental action while entirely in the astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:12:55-07:00","id":1068634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1068626#post1068626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt being in the astral more than just a train of thought tho? Id personally only allow acting in both realms at the same time at higher than mind 1, maybe even not till mastery/making spell that creates a copy of you in the astral. The whole physical thing means that if you have the spell up in the astral you can do a &amp;quot;physical action&amp;quot; and another mental action while entirely in the astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>It moves your consciousness from the outside world to the inner one, your body is still in the outer world though, and One Mind Two Thoughts obviously removes the normal human limitation of being able to maintain only one stream of consciousness at a time so why couldn't one of them stay in your physical body while the other is in your dream body? You use already experiencing a sort of bilocation without using magic. Magic is also able to cross the Astral/Fallen divide so it's not really that extraordinary.<br /> <br /> Yes, obviously the &quot;Physical&quot; Reach clause is referencing what you can do in the Astral, we've been over that. However, it doesn't preclude existing in both planes of existence simultaneously.<br /> <br /> And again, of it doesn't work that way then Dreamspeakers doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T05:48:15-07:00","id":1069268,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> You convinced me finally. Thank you for that.<br /> So with this spell a character broadens himself into to two consciousnesses that can only 'lift' non-heavily-physical actions. Instant the character engages in a mainly physical action his split-self merges to 'lift' it. Here's the trick: each consciousness is free to do any mental task and entering Astral (with this spell) is proved to be just that, mental action that anybody would be capable if he's able to spend mana on threshold.<br /> One 'you' can talk on the phone while the other 'you' enters Astral and when its there it can walk, talk, think. If one of them makes a mainly physical action the other one freezes(? shouldn't it merge and stop being in astral or mentally in material?).<br /> With Reach option 'you' that is in Astral can take one physical action and one mental. Or. 'You' in Astral takes physical action and the 'you' in material takes mental one(physical action can be done only by Astral 'you'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T05:58:01-07:00","id":1069270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1069268#post1069268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&amp;quot;2632&amp;quot;](? shouldn't it merge and stop being in astral or mentally in material?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, for one the spell isn't over, and also leaving the Astral takes a deliberate mental action or having your dream self kicked out by taking too much damage. So it just remains on hold when you're not using it while the spell is still up, barring outside circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:29:09-07:00","id":1078016,"title":"","content":"I hate being late to the party, bit if I can necropost a bit. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> , I mentioned in another topic that Dreamspeakers were giving me problems and you asked me why. In the meantime, I was looking up if anyone had converted them successfully, and it seems you were trying to solve the same problem I was having, that Dreamspeakers do not work without their first attainment, but in 2E the first attainment is either impossible, or is so demanding on reach that you need to put it as a second, third, or maybe even 4th attainment. Which is so awful!<br /> <br /> Here's my primary concern though. You're saying One Mind, Two Thoughts allows one train of thought to remain in the body while the other is in the astral. I'm not entirely convinced. I mean I would prefer you to be right and I can see you won over Moinen, but my concern is that entering the astral realms is basically astral projection, except that while the Mind 4 spell allows you to do such a thing indiscriminately and into the physical world's twilight, entering the astral realms is already a part of the Mage Template as a whole, obviating the need for Mind dots.<br /> <br /> So it seems like Mind 4 is analogous to entering the astral realms, which are part of the mage template and do not follow a clean dot rating. But when you use Astral Projection, your body goes unconscious, similar to how astral travel requires your physical body to go unconscious. One Mind, Two Thoughts originally seems like it wants all your trains of thought to follow where your mind is going. While you can add another train-of-thought to your mind for astral travel, your mind is in the astral, not occupying your physical form at the time--only your brain is left behind, but your magical mind-self has gone elsewhere, and it carries the One Mind, Two Thoughts spell <i>with</i> it.<br /> <br /> Another reason I think this is because the Astral Travel is so mentally taxing--you form basically a goetia of yourself for the journey, you get amnions, and if you die there you get Soul-Shocked. I really think this all means your Mind-self has left your body during Astral Travel and it is unable to leave one thought-process behind and split attention between the physical form and the Mind-self-on-astral-travel.<br /> <br /> My only other thought is that the Dreamspeaker legacy could get away with a <i>very</i> liberal interpretation of &quot;atypical attainments&quot;, but, I do not think that One Mind, Two Thoughts as a praxis is enough to fully duplicate the Dreamspeaker's 1E first attainment even if you spend as much reach as you can.<br /> <br /> Because as I said, dying in the astral leaves you soul-shocked. It sounds more dramatic if it requires ALL your mental processes, including ones tacked on with Compelling magic, otherwise it would be pretty weird if a non-Dreamspeaker Mind Initiate with a demense could pull this trick off, go get a coffee at a cafe, get into a fight in the astral, and suddenly slump over at his table in the cafe from soul-shock.<br /> <br /> Although that might be my tastes... I guess someone else would see that as plenty dramatic? Fitting in with the Dreamspeaker's motiff of looking like madmen/women? But again, I would see that more appropriate for the Dreamspeaker proper and not just any ole initiate of mind?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:26:31-07:00","id":1078036,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> Okay, so when you want to go to the Astral the first thing you need to be able to do is to meditate, which is an extended mental action. If you cast One Mind, Two Thoughts, you can split off a second stream of consciousness from the one that's doing the meditating. The meditating consciousness goes to the Astral, the non-meditating consciousness...doesn't. There's no reason for it to, it's busy doing something else, reading a book perhaps. Essentially, since one stream of consciousness doesn't make the dedicated effort to breach the Astral Barrier, it can't get in, so it gets left outside by default, running your body presumably. Also, to some extent, Mind has brains as part of its purview or Mind damaging spells wouldn't focus on doing actual physical damage. Psychic Assault is my prime example for that. If brains are sort of part of Mind and your actual brains can't go into the Astral then to me it stands to reason that you can have a stream of consciousness active in your physical brain even while another stream is otherwise occupied in the Astral. And again, the Dreamspeakers simply -don't- work unless this is all true, which is the exact problem you're having. Might I suggest following the path of least resistance? <br /> <br /> By the way, you would only need to spend 1 Reach and that's for Advanced Duration, the ritual activation would obviously be the process of meditating into the Astral. That effectively restricts the Dreamspeaker from having a general One Mind, Two Thoughts effect to one that specifically maintains an Astral/Physical divide necessary for the legacy to work. So it works as the very first attainment! Usually Mages get their first two primary attainments at the same time, so the 2nd Mind attainment would probably be something that lets them dive into, and navigate the Astral faster, although it wouldn't bypass the meditation rules completely (If we're hewing to 1e as much as possible).<br /> <br /> As an aside, if you used One Mind, Two Thoughts -before- or combined with Psychic Projection you would end up with one stream of consciousness floating around in Twilight and another stream of consciousness (Man I wish there were a shorter term) running your body. Because I agree, going to the Astral is a form of mental projection, as a result it needs to be subject to the same kind of rule interactions. The Psychic Projection rules are written with the view that -only- this spell was cast, travel to the Astral was written as if this was -all- you're doing. All the spells or abilities are written like that. It doesn't remove the ability for spells to interact in a synergistic manner.<br /> <br /> Moving on, other Mages not in the Dreamspeakers using spells to copy the Dreamspeaker attainments: I don't see a problem with it. Naturally they won't get the attainment benefits of it being impossible to dispel or the automatic activation, etc, but what's the point of being a Dreamspeaker if your Astral travels don't come with a few perks? You say that a Mage suddenly slumping over his table at a cafe isn't dramatic, I say something hella exciting must have happened in the Astral, and if that Mage was a PC it got screen time so it was definitely dramatic. Even if it was an NPC then with a good storyteller it could be dramatic. The important, dramatic thing in that event isn't what happened at the cafe table.<br /> <br /> The whole Soul-Shocked Condition thing: Souls are weird, souls in Mage are especially weird because they're not the seat of personality or anything that we'd typically equate with souls, they seem more like the seat of &quot;humanity&quot; by which we observe that Virtue is supposed to be preeminent and the source of drive. If you're duking it out in the Astral then I think it'd be likely that your sense of drive is typically more engaged there at the moment even if your body is enjoying a nice mocha with your other stream of consciousness. That's where you're invested, that's why you suffer Soul Shock when you get burned in the Astral regardless of your physical activity. If you're in the Fallen and the Astral at the same time, one will inevitably be more eminent. You would have to be crazy (or a Mage) to be involved in a gun battle in the Fallen and a duel in the Astral at the same time, and regardless eventually, survival of your Fallen self or Astral self will have to be prioritized because of the limitations of One Mind, Two Thoughts. A sane Mage (Maybe) would probably prioritize their Fallen self, even though being Soul Shocked will suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:39:24-07:00","id":1078044,"title":"","content":"The mixing of spells to create synergy is a huge boon, but I don't think you can use combined spells as an attainment unless it is the optional arcanum situation. Although if a mage could use combined spells to form the basis of an attainment/rote/praxis that would be amazing.<br /> <br /> I really like your reasoning though. I think showing how it starts from beginning to end was more effective. I could still see someone thinking that one of the thought-lines would still get dragged through into the astral with the other one, but I think you've still made an excellent case. Thank you :3<br /> [insert overused black and white man clapping gif here]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:13:36-07:00","id":1078058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068229-2e-astral-\u2013-how-long-take-journey?p=1078044#post1078044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mixing of spells to create synergy is a huge boon, but I don't think you can use combined spells as an attainment unless it is the optional arcanum situation. Although if a mage could use combined spells to form the basis of an attainment/rote/praxis that would be amazing.<br /> <br /> I really like your reasoning though. I think showing how it starts from beginning to end was more effective. I could still see someone thinking that one of the thought-lines would still get dragged through into the astral with the other one, but I think you've still made an excellent case. Thank you :3<br /> [insert overused black and white man clapping gif here]</div> </div> </div> </div>When talking about Dreamspeakers though it's not necessarily about combined spells, but yes, most the rules are written as standalone and some don't take into account how they might interact with other rules in a synergistic fashion. Anyway, glad I had some good things to say! I've never played a Dreamspeaker but they're one of my favorite legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}